Software versions such as `"1.10.0"` must be compared **numerically**, part by part: `1.10.0` is newer than `1.9.3`, although the string `"1.10.0"` sorts before `"1.9.3"`. Complete the `Version` class so that:

- versions compare with `==`, `!=`, `<`, `<=`, `>` and `>=` numerically (you may assume every version has the same number of parts);
- equal versions have equal hashes, so they can be dict keys and set members;
- comparing with something that is not a `Version` with `==` gives `False` rather than raising.

Keep the `__repr__` as it is.

